WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.510
No translation: 07:31, 08:17, 17:46 {Changes: title added, Line 40 "Balloon shows part of "reception"", Line 64: Some anime translate it as POD (Person on Duty) room}{These lines are quoted by ulrezaj as incomprehensible. 41:explanation, 50:suggestion given, 60:fixed, 76:that's what he means, i have no idea, since kappa are rare (they are legendary in the first place) and he might be implying that what he does even make kappa angry and appear, 98:fixed, 99:fixed, 112:fixed, 118-120, edited the split in the sentence. There was no missing Tl, but the sentence is a bit too long, 262: additional explanation added}

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:42.580
I'm afraid other students returning to the village were caught as well.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:45.120
They might attack again.

00:01:45.490 --> 00:01:45.850
Yeah.

00:01:46.610 --> 00:01:48.280
What's this pungent smell?

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:49.620
Is it the enemy?

00:01:49.620 --> 00:01:51.880
It's nostalgic!

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:57.860
As I thought, you're pickling something.

00:01:58.420 --> 00:02:00.310
Pickling something?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:02.780
Cucumber Commemoration Day is near.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:05.740
Yonezawa-kun will surely be happy.

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.740
What is Cucumber Commemoration Day?

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.740
Beats me.

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.240
That's...

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.750
I am out of asazuke.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:17.410
Translator's note: Asazuke are lightly pickled vegetables.

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:22.730
I... don't give out my pickles to people I don't like...

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:24.220
I see.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:26.960
A shuriken?

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.870
To rust a new weapon...

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.750
You fail as a kunoichi.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.300
Rust makes the pickles delicious!

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.650
Now that you mention it, my grandmother used to put rusted nails in with the pickles.

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.930
I'm sure that you will become a great grandmother.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.710
I'm not even a bride yet, and you're talking about me being a grandmother already?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.960
Now, please come close and look.

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.960
They've come again this year.

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.220
Like previous years, they are back with various rare presentations,

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:08.440
and marvelous illusions that astonish even ninja!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:11.570
Illusion?

00:03:11.900 --> 00:03:14.960
They are travelling performers that come once a year.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.810
The village will be having a festival of sorts during this period.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:19.530
Is it that great?

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.130
Not at all.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:24.770
Kunoichi can't be distracted by those tricks.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:28.490
Since there aren't many festivals here, it attracts people even if it's boring.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:33.860
According to my information, this year's attraction is a magic performance by a great beauty.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:39.360
By the way, the old man of Monjaya is escaping taxes and hiding his seal.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:45.050
Despite the school's closure, the whole town is so carefree, like a snake after its meal.

00:03:45.050 --> 00:03:46.840
Well, that's why...

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.370
Tickets?

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:51.150
It's bad but I will go on a date tonight.

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:52.270
When did you buy them?

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:53.750
And they are the best seats!

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:58.570
Yonezawa-kun gave me these, saying they're to celebrate the commemoration day.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:00.030
He's nice!

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:05.150
I was so happy that I couldn't sleep last night!

00:04:05.150 --> 00:04:06.770
Bad news!

00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:09.830
The school's farm has been desecrated,

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:13.500
and the carp in the principal's room are gone.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.810
First of all, the school is off-limits to boys.

00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:18.670
How did you get that information?

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:21.500
To be outmatched by a kappa, it's the biggest shame of my life.

00:04:18.670 --> 00:04:24.480
Editor's note: A kappa (河童) is a mythical water sprite from Japanese folklore; it can also mean a cucumber.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:26.010
It would be bad if the mountain animals raided the school because they were starving.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:30.350
Yusura-chan, could you ask the animals if they did that?

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.080
Sure, but most likely that's...

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:36.350
Sorry!

00:04:43.830 --> 00:04:44.590
Something the matter?

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:55.340
Just as we thought.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.940
Great catch! Great catch!

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:05.420
Yet you were just starving to the extent that you would eat even poisonous grass.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:08.620
When the school is closed, you do as you wish.

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:11.200
I've got a letter from Principal Yatsugashira.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.530
"Please take care of the school's security.

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.610
There will be a special allowance for you."

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:19.720
What a lavish way of eating.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:23.060
Vegetables and fish are all nature's blessings, you know?

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:24.920
What?

00:05:24.920 --> 00:05:27.350
The uptight kappa has appeared?

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:31.560
That's not the issue!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.920
It's no good, Hayato-dono!

00:05:38.920 --> 00:05:42.420
Yonezawa-kun, please forgive him for my sake.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:45.490
But...!

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:49.100
Hayato is pitiful too.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.040
He was always malnourished.

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:54.220
And he is also a friend of the same forest.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.500
Furthermore, tomorrow is Cucumber Commemoration Day.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.540
Just give him a break, okay?

00:06:02.020 --> 00:06:04.050
Well, if Yusura-chan says so.

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:10.610
Hayato-dono, isn't this good?

00:06:10.610 --> 00:06:13.410
All thanks to Cucumber Commemoration Day.

00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:15.520
Kappa...

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:23.330
Why do they take this long?

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:25.790
They are just kunoichi.

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:28.920
Because they are too good.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:29.860
What?

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:32.030
All that's left is to capture them.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.600
We at least had some achievements last time.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.400
By using this, we will control the villagers.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:43.310
Anyway, they can't lay their hands on the villagers.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:49.920
It's popular!

00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:52.920
Quarrels will surely happen at any festival.

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.510
Those modified ninja might come attacking amidst the fuss.

00:06:56.510 --> 00:06:58.840
There's the possibility that villagers will be pulled into it.

00:06:58.840 --> 00:06:59.430
All right!

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:01.870
Let's patrol and ensure everyone's safety!

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:02.570
Yusura-chan!

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:05.570
Let them be.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.970
There is nothing abnormal.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.290
Anyway, reselling tickets hurts my business.

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:25.930
They're tickets I bought with my measly allowance.

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:27.620
I just sell to whoever wants to buy them.

00:07:27.620 --> 00:07:29.120
It's illegal to steal business.

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:30.800
You evaded tax too!

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:33.660
It's a fight! Fight, fight, fight some more!

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.750
Finished.

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:44.410
W-W-Why...

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.150
Nice to meet you.

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.720
I am Youhi.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:14.380
After the introduction,

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:17.190
I will make the shrine gate over there...

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.240
disappear.

00:08:35.150 --> 00:08:38.530
You are already under my control.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.380
Now, everyone.

00:08:58.630 --> 00:09:00.210
Look.

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:03.000
It's gone.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:03.560
Great!

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.280
Looks like it's finished.

00:09:22.280 --> 00:09:24.860
Maybe we were overanxious?

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:25.780
Any incidents?

00:09:25.780 --> 00:09:27.070
Nothing happened.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:30.950
We fell asleep.

00:09:30.950 --> 00:09:32.320
You drooled.

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:34.870
Where are we going now?

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:38.280
I remembered that I have something to do.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:40.850
Sorry, bye.

00:09:42.580 --> 00:09:45.020
Yonezawa-kun, wait!

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.980
What's wrong with Yonezawa-kun...?

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.540
Even though today's the day...

00:09:51.470 --> 00:09:54.270
I couldn't give him the present.

00:10:10.590 --> 00:10:12.260
I've been waiting...

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:23.370
The festival's over, huh.

00:10:23.370 --> 00:10:25.800
In the end, nothing happened.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:30.840
Monjaya

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.340
I failed.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:34.700
Monsaku-san.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:35.480
There they are!

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:36.950
Capture them!

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:42.950
Let's run for it!

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:45.950
What on earth is this?

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:47.880
Like you will escape!

00:10:47.880 --> 00:10:49.460
What happened?

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:52.670
There they are!

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.570
Let's escape to the forest!

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:00.490
Are they here?

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:02.370
No, they aren't here.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:04.250
Let's search deeper into the forest.

00:11:04.250 --> 00:11:05.280
All right.

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.760
They sure are good at escaping.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:15.430
That's what happened.

00:11:15.430 --> 00:11:18.460
Anyway, the village has become terrible.

00:11:18.810 --> 00:11:21.960
If you get caught, there's no guarantee you'll live.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.700
How on earth did this happen?

00:11:26.270 --> 00:11:28.370
Please stand by here.

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.600
I will go gather information and food.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:33.700
Wait, Yonezawa-kun!

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:38.710
I think they are mass-hypnotized.

00:11:39.000 --> 00:11:42.260
Mass-hypnotizing, a manipulation technique.

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.610
Manipulation technique?

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:48.930
Meaning the villagers' minds are under control, just like a puppet.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.260
Then, did it happen in the tent?

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:54.360
I'm afraid that Yonezawa-kun's been manipulated too.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:57.050
Then Yusura-chan too?

00:11:57.050 --> 00:12:00.990
Looks like for some reason, Yusura hasn't been affected by the spell.

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:03.360
But we must be careful from now on.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.820
What do you mean?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.020
She may abandon us for her man.

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:09.870
No way!

00:12:10.280 --> 00:12:16.840
According to my information, ninety-nine percent of women choose men over friendship.

00:12:16.840 --> 00:12:21.110
In addition, women believe more in fortune-telling based on blood type.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.740
I believe in Yusura-chan.

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:26.790
And in Yonezawa-kun too, of course.

00:12:26.790 --> 00:12:28.920
Something must have gone wrong.

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:31.620
We can't doubt our comrades.

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:35.020
We can't doubt our comrades...

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.130
So, that goes for Takechi-sensei too...

00:12:41.630 --> 00:12:44.810
Something's wrong, I'm sure.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.650
Why have we come here?

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:51.300
Let's escape together, Yusura-chan.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:54.520
If you don't get out of the village, you will get killed.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.820
We both can escape, somehow.

00:12:57.080 --> 00:12:58.160
No way.

00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:01.830
I can't abandon my friends and escape alone.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:06.390
Then, Yusura-chan, will you fight the villagers?

00:13:06.980 --> 00:13:08.380
Let's get out of here.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:10.840
Let's go to a peaceful village and live there.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:18.090
Tonight at cow's hour, I will wait for you at Jizou-sama's statue near the Ryuujin marsh.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:22.560
Translator's note: Cow's hour is between three and five a.m., and Jizou is Ksitigarbha, a bodhisattva.

00:13:18.090 --> 00:13:19.200
See you.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.350
I couldn't sell them.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.520
My debts are...

00:13:42.010 --> 00:13:44.340
Himawari and her gang are wanted?!

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:49.970
What's this?

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.960
Damn it. Where did they go?

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:55.550
One million...!

00:13:57.270 --> 00:13:58.480
Twenty thousand per person.

00:13:58.480 --> 00:14:00.950
As if they are going to be found easily.

00:14:02.410 --> 00:14:04.330
It's their doing.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.860
I have to take cover.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:15.310
Okay.

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:15.870
All right.

00:14:22.590 --> 00:14:24.990
I am hungry.

00:14:24.990 --> 00:14:28.810
What happened to Yonezawa-kun's food?

00:14:28.810 --> 00:14:30.380
Huh? Where is Momota?

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.440
Looks like calling you out with this worked.

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:42.900
Thank you, Hayato-dono.

00:14:43.690 --> 00:14:45.980
Thanks to you, we are saved.

00:14:45.980 --> 00:14:49.290
After all I am the adviser of the Okonomiyaki Club.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.830
There she goes.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:09.050
Like I said, she chose her man.

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:11.260
I'm sure she has her reasons.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:13.650
It's not time for those.

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.490
It's dangerous here. Let's go.

00:15:23.160 --> 00:15:27.600
Tonight at cow's hour, I will wait for you at Jizou-sama's statue near the Ryuujin marsh.

00:15:52.250 --> 00:15:54.690
Too bad, Yusura-chan.

00:15:58.840 --> 00:15:59.930
There they are.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.560
Found you, finally.

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:06.040
Be prepared!

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:26.910
There is no end to them!

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:28.970
We are going to do it!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:33.770
Himeji, no!

00:16:33.770 --> 00:16:35.360
Just use a bamboo sword!

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:37.340
Himeji-san!

00:16:37.340 --> 00:16:38.740
You're mine!

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:40.240
Watch out!

00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:44.500
Yusura-chan!

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.980
You came back!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.110
Let's run! This way!

00:16:49.340 --> 00:16:50.590
Himeji-san.

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.400
You won't get away.

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:02.590
It's time for you to show off your skill.

00:17:15.510 --> 00:17:16.320
A tornado...

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:17.810
...of water?!

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:19.720
This is...!

00:17:23.050 --> 00:17:25.760
I thought they were shuriken, but they are cucumbers.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:27.230
That's...

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:28.280
It can't be!

00:17:31.730 --> 00:17:32.860
Yonezawa-kun!

00:17:33.620 --> 00:17:36.370
What?! He looks like an assassin.

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.960
Yonezawa-kun, please stop!

00:17:40.960 --> 00:17:42.010
It's no use.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.560
Yonezawa-kun is also controlled by somebody.

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:46.440
Although I don't want to believe it...

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:47.660
That can't be true!

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:52.000
Because Yonezawa-kun said he wanted to escape with me.

00:17:52.000 --> 00:17:54.450
If he really were being controlled by somebody,

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:56.300
he wouldn't have said that.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:00.810
Not completely,

00:18:00.810 --> 00:18:03.260
but half of his heart is being controlled.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:06.230
Half of his heart? What do you mean?

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:25.030
He sleeps with his eyes half-open.

00:18:25.030 --> 00:18:31.070
According to my information, those who sleep with eyes half-open are pure.

00:18:32.730 --> 00:18:35.490
It means that the manipulation technique wasn't complete.

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.400
Then there could be a way...

00:18:38.130 --> 00:18:41.540
Yonezawa-kun, we're not the real enemy.

00:18:41.540 --> 00:18:43.270
Please, remember!

00:18:44.770 --> 00:18:46.240
Hayato-dono, here!

00:18:52.320 --> 00:18:53.410
Hayato-dono!

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.290
It's her!

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:13.630
It we don't catch her, the spell on Yonezawa-kun won't break!

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:15.470
Stop!

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:17.460
Don't stand in my way!

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:22.780
Yonezawa-kun, wake up!

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:25.550
I am out of asazuke.

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:27.240
At least give me one...

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:28.980
Thank you, Tsukiyohime.

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.270
Hey Yonezawa-kun, do you remember?

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.740
The day when we first met?

00:19:46.670 --> 00:19:48.940
The one with thorns...

00:19:48.940 --> 00:19:50.100
Thorns...

00:19:53.440 --> 00:19:54.950
There it is!

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.220
The fated meeting at the cucumber farm.

00:20:06.000 --> 00:20:07.200
And also...

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:12.810
The day we discovered our true feelings.

00:20:13.450 --> 00:20:16.130
That's our Cucumber Commemoration Day.

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.650
From that day on, I'll...

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:26.200
Please, please remember!

00:20:26.200 --> 00:20:29.140
Please return to your original self!

00:20:34.430 --> 00:20:36.710
You. What did you...?!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:40.130
I threw a shuriken too!

00:20:53.680 --> 00:20:55.690
My head is blank.

00:20:55.690 --> 00:20:57.770
Don't look.

00:20:57.770 --> 00:21:00.240
We have to close our eyes.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:03.400
Yonezawa-kun, hang on!

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.980
Sorry, I...

00:21:08.200 --> 00:21:12.150
This nostalgic feeling fills my heart.

00:21:12.150 --> 00:21:15.190
I finally remembered, Yusura-chan.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:17.720
My cherished...

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:23.000
Yonezawa-kun!

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:28.770
You got him already.

00:21:30.450 --> 00:21:31.970
You!

00:21:32.740 --> 00:21:33.730
Himawari.

00:21:33.730 --> 00:21:34.600
Close your eyes!

00:21:34.840 --> 00:21:36.840
Give way! Give way!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.350
A chance!

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:04.170
Please.

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:05.370
Wake up!

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:12.240
Looks like he's sleeping.

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.310
He accepted the gift.

00:22:19.980 --> 00:22:23.350
T-The present saved his life!

00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:26.840
Thank goodness!

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:30.030
Love conquers all!

00:22:44.550 --> 00:22:46.370
Dawn already...

00:22:46.370 --> 00:22:48.320
I am touched by something.

00:22:48.320 --> 00:22:50.390
That would be Momota...

00:22:50.390 --> 00:22:53.050
They're beautiful, these morning clouds.

00:22:53.690 --> 00:22:59.250
I'm out of asazuke, at least give me one...

00:24:11.240 --> 00:24:13.640
Shinobi High School is on fire!

00:24:13.640 --> 00:24:19.200
With the help of Nanafushi-san, we somehow managed to take cover in the forest, but...

00:24:19.200 --> 00:24:23.400
running like this makes us hungry, cold, and the enemies keep coming after us.

00:24:24.070 --> 00:24:28.230
So, I will stay behind in the forest with Tsukiyohime-san and fight.

00:24:28.230 --> 00:24:29.220
Huh?

00:24:29.220 --> 00:24:30.950
There are two of Tsukiyohime-san?

00:24:31.780 --> 00:24:32.640
Next time:

00:24:32.640 --> 00:24:35.050
"The moonlit forest is full of dangers."

00:24:35.400 --> 00:24:38.770
Hayato-dono, do you have anybody that you want to protect?
